CORE broken-z3-smt-backend broken-smt-backend no-new-smt thorough-paths
main.c
--no-standard-checks
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
broken-z3-smt-backend: --z3 uses QF_AUFBV (bitvector, not FPA), so
the 10 double-precision fmod calls produce a huge formula that Z3
cannot solve within the test timeout.
no-new-smt: incremental SMT2 backend does not support floatbv_mod.
thorough-paths: --paths lifo with 10 assertions takes >5 minutes
because each path builds a 282-bit integer significand divider.
